</script><![endif]--><meta name="description" content="The Gravity Recovery and Climate Experiment Follow-On (GRACE-FO) mission, a joint partnership between NASA and the German Research Centre for Geosciences (GFZ), launched on 22 May 2018. It uses twin satellites to accurately map month-to-month variations in the Earth&#039;s gravity field and surface mass changes. It will continue the legacy data record of the first Gravity Recovery" />
