<div id="block-block-14" class="block block-block last even">

  <div class="block-content">
              
    <div class="full-width-container" style="background-color: #4fb4db ; font-size: 14px; color: #ffffff; padding-left: 10px; padding-right: 10px; padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; "><strong>  IMPORTANT UPDATE</strong>: We are in the process of migrating this PO.DAAC website into <a href="https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/centers/po-daac">Earthdata</a>. Thank you for your patience as we make this transition. <a href="https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/about/web-unification-project">Read about the Web Unification Project</a>. </div>

<p><!--
<div class="messages error" style="background: #fef5f1; color: #8c2e0b; border: 1px solid #ed541d; border-radius: 7px;">
<p><strong><span style="background-color:rgb(254, 245, 241); color:rgb(140, 46, 11)">SYSTEM ALERT</span></strong>:&nbsp;PO.DAAC will have an approximately 10-hour ingest and archive downtime due to maintenance. SWOT data: Jan 13, 2026 (~7AM&ndash;5 PM PT). Non-SWOT data: Jan 14, 2026 (~7AM&ndash;5PM PT). Data remains searchable and accessible via Earthdata Cloud.&nbsp; We apologize for the inconvenience.</p>


<p><strong><span style="background-color:rgb(254, 245, 241); color:rgb(140, 46, 11)">DATA ALERT:</span></strong> Temporary Issue with DSWx-S1 Data: Between May 20, 2025 and Nov 7, 2025, the Dynamic Surface Water&nbsp;eXtent&nbsp;from Sentinel-1 (DSWx-S1) product was affected by a processing issue that resulted in Sentinel-1A and Sentinel-1C data acquired on different dates occasionally being combined into a single product. After a software fix issued on Dec 9, 2025, all DSWx-S1 data going forward resumed normalcy. OPERA is in the process of replacing and reproducing impacted DSWx-S1 between May 20, 2025 and Dec 9, 2025 and expect to complete these tasks by Jan. 2026.</p>
</div>


<p>Anomaly affecting the OPERA DSWx-S1 product: OPERA has discovered a processing error affecting DSWx-S1 data products generated from May 2025 onwards. This error is causing Sentinel-1A (S1A) and Sentinel-1C (S1C) data to be incorrectly mixed into a single product. This issue is currently under investigation by the OPERA team. As a precaution, the OPERA team has temporarily stopped the production of DSWx-S1 while they resolve this matter. We will provide more information as soon as it becomes available. We apologize for any inconvenience this may cause.&nbsp;</p>


SYSTEM ALERT: 12/4/25 - The system is currently experiencing an issue resulting in some data being unavailable. Granule Search is degraded, and the most recently ingested data products will not appear in search results until the system is fully restored.
<div class="messages error" style="background: #fef5f1; color: #8c2e0b; border: 1px solid #ed541d; border-radius: 7px;">
<h3 class="rtecenter"><strong>SYSTEM ALERT:</strong> PO.DAAC will have a 48-hour data ingest and archive downtime.&nbsp;Non-SWOT data will be affected on July 21, 2025, and SWOT data on July 22, 2025. During this period, no data will be ingested, processed, or archived. We apologize for the inconvenience.</h3>

<h3 class="rtecenter">NASA&#39;s Common Metadata Repository (CMR) Search Integrity encountered a service degradation, resulting in an outage from May 12 to May 14, 2025, which caused a downstream impact on PO.DAAC Data Holdings. CMR is currently operating without any known issues.</h3>

<p>texr: PO.DAAC will have a 72-hours ingest and archive downtime for SWOT data from 12/9-12/11 2024, and Non-SWOT data from 12/10-12/24 2024. During this time, no data will be ingested, processed and archived. We apologize for the inconvenience.</p>

<p>TEXT: PO.DAAC Portal may experience intermittent downtime during the scheduled System Maintenance window (May&nbsp;30, 2024, between 11am-1pm PST). We apologize for the inconvenience.</p>

<h3 class="rtecenter" style="color:rgb(140, 46, 11)"><strong>Dataset Search and Discovery is currently experiencing an unexpected system outage. Datasets are unavailable at this time. Access will be restored as soon as possible.&nbsp;</strong></h3>
may experience intermittent slowdown during the scheduled maintenance window today Sep 25, 2023 TEXT: PO.DAAC Portal may experience intermittent downtime during the scheduled System Maintenance window (November 30, 2023, between 11:00am-11:30am PST). We apologize for the inconvenience.

<p>&nbsp;</p>
PO.DAAC will be performing a major software upgrade on our Cloud Ingest System on Monday 5/20/24 from 2pm to 6pm PDT. No new granules will show up in any of the Cloud tools/services during the upgrade.

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>TEXT: Our MUR datasets&amp;rsquo; daily generation is delayed this week due to an upgrade to our production machine. We are actively working on this and aim to restore daily generation by Friday (this includes generating granules for Sep 9 &amp;ndash; 12 and beyond).&amp;nbsp;Thank you for your patience.</p>

<div class="messages error" style="background: #fef5f1; color: #8c2e0b; border: 1px solid #ed541d; border-radius: 7px;">
<p class="rtecenter"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong>REMINDER:&nbsp; PO.DAAC Drive and the Legacy Data Access Tools and Services (specifically LAS, CWS, THREDDS) retired on April 24, 2023.</strong></span></p>

<div class="messages error" style="background: #fef5f1; color: #8c2e0b; border: 1px solid #ed541d; border-radius: 7px;">
<p class="rtecenter"><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; SYSTEM ALERT:</strong><em><strong>&nbsp;</strong></em>&nbsp;Outage: An Amazon Web Services outage is affecting our Common Metadata Repository, Earthdata Search and Metadata Maintenance Tool services. You may see search failures during this period. We do not currently have an estimate on when this issue will be resolved</p>
</div>

<div class="messages error" style="background: #fef5f1; color: #8c2e0b; border: 1px solid #ed541d; border-radius: 7px;">
<p class="rtecenter"><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp; SYSTEM ALERT:</strong><em><strong>&nbsp;</strong></em> The PO.DAAC HiTIDE is currently experiencing problems. The subsetting capability is unavailable at this time. We apologize for the inconvenience.</p>

<p class="rtecenter"><strong>SYSTEM ALERT:</strong><em><strong>&nbsp;</strong></em><span style="background-color:rgb(254, 245, 241); color:rgb(140, 46, 11)">&nbsp; PO.DAAC&nbsp; is experiencing some technical issues relating to data download. We are aware of the issue and are investigating the causes. We apologize for the inconvenience.</span></p>
</div>

<div class="messages error" style="background: #fef5f1; color: #8c2e0b; border: 1px solid #ed541d; border-radius: 7px;">
<h3 class="rtecenter">The PO.DAAC State of the Ocean (SOTO) will be temporarily unavailable during the scheduled upgrade window on Wednesday, March 10, 2021 between 2pm - 3pm PST.</h3>

<h3 class="rtecenter">We apologize for the inconvenience.</h3>
</div>

<p>--&gt;</p>
</div>

<p>&nbsp;</p>

<p>--&gt;</p>

<p>--&gt;</p>

<p>--&gt;</p>
--&gt;</div>

<p>--&gt;</p>
--></p>
